# Flatpaks chosen deliberately, on top of the pacman manifest.
#
# This is the Flatpak half of the manifest. `packages/chosen.packages` covers the
# pacman repos and the AUR; neither it nor `packages.txt` can see a Flatpak, so an
# app installed this way appears in no other file (see Source, in CONTEXT.md).
#
# Reach for a Flatpak only when neither `omarchy install <thing>` nor
# `omarchy pkg add <packages...>` covers the app -- it is not packaged for Arch, it
# is proprietary, or it is worth sandboxing. See ADR-0032.
#
# Format: one application ID per line, # comments. `loaf flatpaks` diffs this file
# against what is installed, and installs what is missing with --install.
#
# Installs are system-wide, matching the system-level flathub remote.

# Minecraft launcher. Not in the Arch repos; the AUR build is a wrapper around the
# same upstream binary, so the Flatpak is the lower-maintenance route.
gg.dawn.Launcher
